{
  "name": "Find companies that match your market, score them with AI and keep the best in a sheet",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Find companies that match your market, score them with AI and keep the best in a sheet\n\n### How it works\nA weekly shortlist of accounts worth your time. Argorant searches companies in your industry, country and size range and returns up to max_companies of them with industry, size, location and description. Companies scored in an earlier run are skipped. Your own AI model scores each new one from 1 to 10 against your ideal customer. Companies at or above min_score land in your sheet with domain, name, score and reason.\n\nArgorant search is free. Your model provider bills its own usage.\n\n### Setup\n1. Install the community node **n8n-nodes-argorant** (tested with 0.3.0 on n8n 2.46.6): Settings > Community nodes > Install. Guide: https://github.com/argorant/n8n-nodes-argorant\n2. Add an **Argorant API** credential with a key from Argorant (Settings, API keys).\n3. Set industry (an Argorant industry such as Software & Internet), country, size, max_companies, ideal_customer and min_score in **Settings**.\n4. Create a sheet with the columns domain, company, score, reason, industry, size and pick it in **Add to the shortlist**.\n5. Pick a chat model (any chat model node works) and activate.\n\n### Customization\nAdd a Lead Count per company to see how many buyers each one has.",
        "height": 636,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 1
      },
      "id": "c7d65e43-af0c-494f-a801-1c2fadad6779",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -620,
        -260
      ]
    },
    {
